cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below and the DOI of the archived Zenodo release."
title: "Monte Carlo Simulation of 2D Bearing-Only Object Localization Using Weighted and Unweighted Nonlinear Least Squares"
authors:
  - family-names: "Terentiev"
    given-names: "Oleksandr"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oterentiev/bearing-only-localization-monte-carlo"
abstract: >-
  Python software implementing a Monte Carlo simulation framework for
  two-dimensional bearing-only object localization. It compares weighted
  and unweighted nonlinear least-squares estimators for three- and
  four-station observation configurations and reports accuracy and
  covariance-based uncertainty metrics.
keywords:
  - bearing-only localization
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - weighted least squares
  - ordinary least squares
  - nonlinear estimation
  - position estimation
  - uncertainty analysis
